# Implementation Plan - Project-Ready Template System with Ready-to-Use Graphify Integration

Transform the repository into a **project-ready template system**. When a developer creates a new project from this template, all required agents, skills, architecture plans, cross-platform automation, Git ignore rules, Docker configurations, and **Graphify integrations** (configuration, skills, tool entry points, post-commit hooks, ignore rules) are automatically configured and ready to use without manual boilerplate.

---

## Key Architecture Principles & Requirements

1. **Strict Safety**: Read-only reference inspection of `weighingscale_app`, `rawadhai_backend`, and `rawadhai_frontend`. **NEVER** edit, rename, move, or modify any files in those three projects. All modifications take place exclusively within this template repository (`myproject_agent_skill_prompt_files`).
2. **Framework Isolation**: Maintain 100% self-contained framework directories (`django/`, `flutter/`, `react/`, `vuejs/`, `wordpress/`). No cross-framework file dependencies.
3. **Project Instantiation & Bootstrapping**: Provide automated cross-platform setup scripts (`automation/linux/setup-project.sh`, `automation/windows/setup-project.ps1`, `automation/macos/setup-project.sh`) to initialize a new project from this template, selecting the target framework and setting up Graphify, Git hooks, Docker, and AI tool configurations.
4. **Ready-to-Use Graphify Integration**:
   - Generated projects receive complete Graphify files: `.graphifyignore`, framework-specific Graphify skill, tool entry points (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, `.codex/instructions.md`, `.antigravity/README.md`), installation scripts, and post-commit hook integration (`post-commit.sh`, `post-commit.ps1`).
   - Ignores local build/cache data (`graphify-out/cache/`) while tracking project graph metadata (`graphify-out/graph.json`).
   - Compatible with Antigravity, Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and VS Code.
5. **Modular Graphify Disabling**: Graphify can be enabled or cleanly disabled/removed (`--no-graphify` flag or `clean-graphify.sh` / `clean-graphify.ps1`) without breaking the rest of the agent/skill system.
6. **No Hardcoded Values**: All scripts, configurations, and skills dynamically use the target project's path and framework. Zero hardcoded project names.
7. **10-Step Generic Agent Workflow**: Add generic agent entry points and workflows that automatically evaluate codebase size/unfamiliarity, run Graphify if useful, select framework agent + skills + architecture plans, implement, test, and review.
8. **Cross-Platform First-Class Automation**: Separate Linux (`.sh`), macOS (`.sh`), and Windows (`.ps1`, `.cmd`) cleanly. PowerShell scripts do not depend on Bash; Bash scripts do not depend on Windows commands.
9. **Optional Git Hooks**: Developers can select Git hooks mode (`OFF`, `basic`, `full`). Never silently auto-install hooks.
10. **Actionable Development Coverage (>= 30%)**: All skills provide concrete rules (`What to inspect`, `What to do`, `What not to do`, `What tools/commands to use`, `What files to modify`, `How to validate the result`).

